<title>HONG KONG: HK's Chan to chair group promoting HK-U.S. trade.</title>
<headline>HK's Chan to chair group promoting HK-U.S. trade.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ronnie Chan, chairman of Hang Lung Development Co Ltd and Amoy Properties Ltd, will be the new chairman of the Hong Kong/United States Economic Cooperation Committee, the Hong Kong Trade Development Council (TDC) said on Monday.</p>
<p>The committee, created by the government-funded TDC, promotes trade and investment between Hong Kong and the U.S.</p>
<p>Chan succeeds Tung Chee-hwa, who stepped down as chairman of the Hong Kong Committee upon when he was selected the leader of post-colonial Hong Kong, the statement said.</p>
<p>The British colony reverts to China on July 1.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6590</p>
</text>
